<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">prospect</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">prospect</ansi>

Read the rock in a cave, on a mountainside or along a cliff: what ore runs
here, what it is good for, and how much is left. If the seam is worked out,
it tells you roughly when it will be worth digging again, and it tells you
when the rock is too hard for your pick.

Copper, tin, coal and iron anyone can name. Silver, basalt-iron and lake-iron
take a sharp eye, and gold a sharper one: your <ansi fg="yellow">Perception</ansi> decides whether
you know what you are looking at. You can mine an ore you cannot name; you
just will not know what it is until it is out.

